From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:59:12 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 25/83] Plutonium: agents drive windows and tabs over DevTools

EXO-AGENT: the Plutonium DevTools domain (cros_protocol.pdl) on the browser
target, for trusted clients only (the session's --remote-debugging-port,
which the helper uses). The helper drives the shells' windows and tabs with
it, without a shell page:
- Tabs and windows as lists and events; createTab (PlutoniumTabs::
  CreateAgentTab, opened by "agent"), navigateTab, tabCommand,
  answerTabDialog, captureTab; captureWindow, closeWindow, resizeWindow.
- Window input: dispatchWindowMouseEvent and dispatchWindowKeyEvents.
  EmbeddedWindows::InjectMouseEvent() sends a page-like event without moving
  the parked window or focusing it; InjectKeyEvents() lends the window
  keyboard focus (standing in for the focused aura window) for the keys,
  which go through Seat::DispatchAgentKeyEvent() with their physical code.
- Frame rate: viz slows frame sinks nothing draws to a frame a second, and
  a parked window no page shows is never drawn. KeepDrawing() submits its
  frames with may_throttle_if_undrawn_frames off (setWindowAwake, and
  screencasts); setTabAwake keeps a hidden tab rendering (hidden capture),
  for Playwright, which waits on frames before each action.
- Window screencasts (plutonium_agent.cc): each commit copied as Snapshot()
  does, one at a time and at most 30 a second, with ack pacing. A video
  capturer saw no damage on an undrawn window and refreshed every 200 ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
